+## Failed session startup
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model work runs. `afterSession` is cleanup for an attempted turn, not evidence that startup succeeded: allocation may be partial, so hooks must track what they acquired and tolerate resources never being allocated ([validated by: reports a beforeSession failure and cleans up before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
